{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3253","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3253","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3253\",\"parent_revision\":\"48e224d615ae60f96c40fb606be39d9a07d316dc23433cb7c56a3e93794e559c\",\"root_revision\":\"48e224d615ae60f96c40fb606be39d9a07d316dc23433cb7c56a3e93794e559c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-27\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nplugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/swarm.md instructs two teammates to write a different literal vocabulary than plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md's Output Validation Gate checks for in the same section. Both instances were observed in the same grooming run (backlog item #3244):\\n\\n1. **Design Intent Alignment.** swarm.md's Teammates list (item 6, alignment-analyst) instructs: \\\"leading the section with a MISSION_ALIGNED or MISSION_DIVERGENT verdict line.\\\" finalize.md's Output Validation Gate required-sections table requires: \\\"Contains `Alignment assessment:` field with ALIGNED/DIVERGENT/NOT_APPLICABLE.\\\" Neither the literal string \\\"Alignment assessment:\\\" nor the bare tokens ALIGNED/DIVERGENT/NOT_APPLICABLE (as opposed to MISSION_ALIGNED/MISSION_DIVERGENT) appear when alignment-analyst follows swarm.md's own instruction exactly.\\n\\n2. **RT-ICA.** Neither swarm.md nor rtica-assessor.md's own agent definition specifies an exact literal vocabulary for the RT-ICA teammate's final-assessment output; in the observed run, rtica-assessor's report led \\\"## Verdict: **READY**\\\". finalize.md's Output Validation Gate requires the section to contain the literal string \\\"Decision: APPROVED\\\" or \\\"Decision: BLOCKED\\\" plus \\\"Date: YYYY-MM-DD\\\". \\\"Verdict: READY\\\" satisfies neither literal requirement.\\n\\nIn both cases the orchestrator had to add a small patch entry to the section containing the exact literal field finalize.md's gate scans for, after independently verifying the teammate's underlying analysis was substantively correct \u2014 the analysis itself was not wrong, only the reporting vocabulary was inconsistent between the two workflow documents that are supposed to agree on it.\\n\\n**Not yet checked**: whether the same mismatch affects any of the other six required-sections table rows (RT-ICA, Impact Radius, Fact-Check, Acceptance Criteria, Reproducibility, Issue Classification, Priority) \u2014 Priority's stated requirement (\\\"Contains `Effort:` field\\\") is itself an odd cross-reference to a different section name and was not independently checked in this run.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 hit twice consecutively while running the groom workflow against #3244; the orchestrator's Output Validation Gate pass caught both, but only because the orchestrator was reading the actual literal content rather than trusting the teammates' own STATUS reports\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-27\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Third Instance Confirmed\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-27T05:29:48.937066Z</sub>\\n\\nChecked the previously-flagged \\\"not yet checked\\\" Priority/Effort cross-reference in this same #3244 run \u2014 it is also broken, a third instance of the same pattern. finalize.md's required-sections table states: \\\"Priority | Contains `Effort:` field\\\". Neither groomer's actual Priority section content nor its separate Effort section (both produced exactly as swarm.md's groomer prompt specifies \u2014 free-form prose, no \\\"Effort:\\\" label) contain the literal string \\\"Effort:\\\". The table's row appears to conflate the Priority and Effort sections, or the literal-string check itself needs to accept either section, or be dropped for prose-content sections in favor of a non-empty check (matching how Reproducibility, Impact, Benefits, Expected Behavior, Files, Resources, Dependencies are already treated as free-form/non-empty-only per the table's own \\\"Optional sections (not validated for presence)\\\" list \u2014 Effort and Priority are asymmetric with that treatment for no stated reason).\\n\\nSame orchestrator workaround applied: patched #3244's Priority section with a literal \\\"Effort:\\\" line to satisfy the mechanical check.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"166cb4278b76830f3af74f7110419e91d792dafd1e5e4f6d28448e05a7ed54d5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQ_Bfww\"}"}